{"seq":87,"slug":"fault-tolerance-resilience-patterns","title":"容错与韧性模式","stage":"DONE","category":"cs-fundamentals","chapterCount":4,"docCount":12,"url":"/h/cs-fundamentals/fault-tolerance-resilience-patterns","rating":{"composite":3.92,"verdict":"stable","groups":{"quality":3.6,"coverage":3.5,"positioning":4,"strategic":4.67},"weights":{"quality":0.3,"coverage":0.25,"positioning":0.2,"strategic":0.25},"profile":null},"introMarkdown":"# 容错与韧性模式\n\n任何运行在真实世界里的分布式系统，迟早都会遇到网络丢包、机器宕机、依赖超时、流量洪峰这些「不可避免」的事。容错与韧性不是为了消灭故障——故障消灭不掉——而是让系统在故障发生时仍能交付可接受的服务，并在故障过去后自我恢复。这个 hub 把这套思想拆成四条互相递进的主线，从「为什么」一路讲到「怎么做、怎么验证」。\n\n第一条主线是**基础**。在动手写任何模式之前，先要把语言对齐：故障到底有哪些类型（崩溃、遗漏、时序、拜占庭），失效是如何在系统里级联传播的，以及我们用什么数字来谈论可靠性（可用性、MTBF、MTTR、SLI/SLO/错误预算）。没有这套度量，「系统更可靠了」只是一句无法证伪的口号。基础这一章为后面所有模式提供共同的词汇与判据。\n\n第二条主线是**核心模式**。这是工程师日常打交道最多的部分：重试与退避如何在不放大故障的前提下吸收瞬时错误，断路器如何在依赖持续失败时快速失败、给下游喘息之机，超时与舱壁隔离如何把「一个慢依赖拖垮整个进程」的风险关进笼子里。这三个模式常常组合使用，它们共同回答一个问题：当依赖不可靠时，调用方该如何自保。\n\n第三条主线是**降级与隔离**。当资源真的不够、或下游真的崩了，光靠重试和断路是不够的，系统必须主动做减法：用回退值或降级路径维持核心功能，用负载卸除和限流在过载前丢弃低价值请求，用幂等与去重让重试和重复投递不至于造成二次伤害。这一章关注的是「在压力下如何优雅地少做事」，而不是「假装什么都能做」。\n\n第四条主线是**工程实践**。模式写对了不等于系统韧性强——你得能验证它。这一章讲混沌工程与故障注入如何主动暴露弱点，面向故障的可观测性如何让你在事故中快速定位根因，以及那些看似合理实则危险的反模式（重试风暴、同步级联、共享线程池耗尽）如何识别与规避。\n\n四条主线的关系是：基础给判据，模式给手段，降级给底线，实践给闭环。建议按章顺序阅读；若你已有分布式系统经验，也可以从你正在踩的坑所在的章节切入，再回溯到基础补齐度量语言。\n","chapters":[{"seq":1,"slug":"foundations","title":"基础","docCount":3,"url":"/h/cs-fundamentals/fault-tolerance-resilience-patterns/foundations","docs":[{"seq":1,"slug":"why-resilience","title":"为何需要韧性","url":"/h/cs-fundamentals/fault-tolerance-resilience-patterns/foundations/why-resilience"},{"seq":2,"slug":"failure-models","title":"故障模型与失效模式","url":"/h/cs-fundamentals/fault-tolerance-resilience-patterns/foundations/failure-models"},{"seq":3,"slug":"reliability-metrics","title":"可靠性度量","url":"/h/cs-fundamentals/fault-tolerance-resilience-patterns/foundations/reliability-metrics"}]},{"seq":2,"slug":"patterns","title":"核心模式","docCount":3,"url":"/h/cs-fundamentals/fault-tolerance-resilience-patterns/patterns","docs":[{"seq":1,"slug":"retry-and-backoff","title":"重试与退避","url":"/h/cs-fundamentals/fault-tolerance-resilience-patterns/patterns/retry-and-backoff"},{"seq":2,"slug":"circuit-breaker","title":"断路器","url":"/h/cs-fundamentals/fault-tolerance-resilience-patterns/patterns/circuit-breaker"},{"seq":3,"slug":"timeout-and-bulkhead","title":"超时与舱壁隔离","url":"/h/cs-fundamentals/fault-tolerance-resilience-patterns/patterns/timeout-and-bulkhead"}]},{"seq":3,"slug":"degradation","title":"降级与隔离","docCount":3,"url":"/h/cs-fundamentals/fault-tolerance-resilience-patterns/degradation","docs":[{"seq":1,"slug":"fallback-and-graceful-degradation","title":"回退与优雅降级","url":"/h/cs-fundamentals/fault-tolerance-resilience-patterns/degradation/fallback-and-graceful-degradation"},{"seq":2,"slug":"load-shedding-rate-limiting","title":"负载卸除与限流","url":"/h/cs-fundamentals/fault-tolerance-resilience-patterns/degradation/load-shedding-rate-limiting"},{"seq":3,"slug":"idempotency-and-dedup","title":"幂等与去重","url":"/h/cs-fundamentals/fault-tolerance-resilience-patterns/degradation/idempotency-and-dedup"}]},{"seq":4,"slug":"practice","title":"工程实践","docCount":3,"url":"/h/cs-fundamentals/fault-tolerance-resilience-patterns/practice","docs":[{"seq":1,"slug":"resilience-testing","title":"韧性测试","url":"/h/cs-fundamentals/fault-tolerance-resilience-patterns/practice/resilience-testing"},{"seq":2,"slug":"observability-for-failures","title":"面向故障的可观测性","url":"/h/cs-fundamentals/fault-tolerance-resilience-patterns/practice/observability-for-failures"},{"seq":3,"slug":"antipatterns","title":"反模式与陷阱","url":"/h/cs-fundamentals/fault-tolerance-resilience-patterns/practice/antipatterns"}]}]}